SUMMARY:Week 2026-19 - Lower Strength + Sled Development
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Build lower body strength and Hyrox sled power without excessive fatigue carryover.\n\nWARM-UP 10 min: Hip circles x10 each direction\, glute bridges 2x15 (2-sec hold)\, goblet squat 2x10 light (2-sec pause)\, ankle rotations x10 each\, banded clamshells 2x15 each side.\n\nBACK SQUAT — 4x5 @ RPE 7 (approx 80–87kg). 3 min rest. Brace 360 degrees\, knees track toes\, hip crease below knee\, drive floor away. No torso collapse. If bar drifts forward\, reduce load. Log weight and RPE.\n\nROMANIAN DEADLIFT — 4x6 @ RPE 7 (approx 75–85kg). 2.5 min rest. Push hips back not down\, neutral spine\, feel hamstrings load before reversing\, bar within 5cm of legs. Log weight and RPE.\n\nWALKING LUNGE — 3x20m @ 40kg. 2 min rest. Upright torso\, rear knee hovers 2cm from floor\, drive through front heel\, lead knee does not cave.\n\nSLED PUSH — 6x15m moderate load\, 60 sec rest. Lean ~45 degrees\, short powerful strides\, balls of feet\, full hip extension each step.\n\nSLED PULL — 6x15m moderate load\, 60 sec rest. Face away from sled\, drive arms back\, upright posture\, quick short steps\, lean slightly back to keep rope tension.\n\nCORE FINISHER — 3 rounds\, 45 sec rest between: Plank 60 sec (brace all three planes) + side plank 30 sec each side (hips stacked and high) + dead bug 10 reps (lower back pinned).\n\nKPI: No form breakdown across any set. Squat depth consistent. Sled pace steady. Log all working weights.
